exports[`fscale hooks install > --all tries every file: it writes the ones it can, and says which it refused > claude and cursor: stderr 1`] = `
"fscale: checking that the hook can start: running \`npx --yes firescale@0.5.3 --version --json\` in the repo root, as an agent would. npx may download firescale from the npm registry first.
fscale: .claude/settings.json was left as it is: the stop hook cannot go in as new lines, and firescale does not rewrite lines you wrote. The file, or the object or list the hook goes into, is written on one line or is null. Put its brackets on their own lines and run this again, or add it by hand. Add this item to the list "hooks.Stop" by hand:

{
  "hooks": [
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command": "npx --yes firescale@0.5.3 hooks run --agent claude"
    }
  ]
}

Then run this again to check it.
fscale: .cursor/hooks.json was left as it is: the stop hook cannot go in as new lines, and firescale does not rewrite lines you wrote. The file, or the object or list the hook goes into, is written on one line or is null. Put its brackets on their own lines and run this again, or add it by hand. Add "version": 1 at the top level and this item to the list "hooks.stop" by hand:

{
  "command": "npx --yes firescale@0.5.3 hooks run --agent cursor"
}

Then run this again to check it.
"
`;

